Id: con020c
Severity: CONFIG
Category: tigris
Check: config tiger tigris
Fix: Merge the settings you want to keep into tigris.conf and remove tigerrc (or keep tigerrc and remove tigris.conf).
References: tigris(8)

The configuration directory holds both tigerrc, the name before 4.0,
and tigris.conf, and only one of them is read: the tigerrc, unless it
was not accepted (con003c, con015c), in which case the tigris.conf.
The old name wins so that an upgrade which installs a new tigris.conf
beside a tigerrc the admin edited does not switch their settings back
to the defaults; a .deb upgraded from 3.9.0 keeps /etc/tigris/tigerrc
and adds /etc/tigris/tigris.conf, for instance. Edits to the file that
is not read have no effect. Tiger_* settings copied from a tigerrc
work in tigris.conf as they are.
